  "text": "We are asked to find the **positive difference between the largest and second-largest prime factors** of the number **407707**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Factorize 407707\n\nWe need to find the **prime factorization** of 407707.\n\nLet’s try dividing by small primes:\n\n- 407707 is **odd**, so not divisible by 2.\n- **Sum of digits**: 4 + 0 + 7 + 7 + 0 + 7 = 25 → not divisible by 3.\n- **Ends in 7**, not divisible by 5.\n- Try dividing by 7:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 7 = 58243.857\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 11:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 11 = 37064.27\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 13:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 13 = 31362.07\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 17:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 17 = 23982.76\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 19:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 19 = 21458.26\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 23:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 23 = 17726.39\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 29:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 29 = 14058.86\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 31:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 31 = 13151.84\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 37:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 37 = 11019.108\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 41:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 41 = 9944.073\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 43:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 43 = 9479.28\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 47:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 47 = 8674.59\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 53:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 53 = 7692.58\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 59:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 59 = 6919.71\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 61:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 61 = 6689.36\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 67:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 67 = 6085.17\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 71:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 71 = 5742.35\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 73:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 73 = 5585.02\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 79:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 79 = 5159.58\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 83:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 83 = 4909.66\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nTry 89:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 89 = 4581.0\\ldots \\quad \\text{Yes!}\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n407707 \\div 89 = 4581\n$$\n\nNow check if 4581 is divisible by 89:\n\n$$\n4581 \\div 89 = 51.47\\ldots \\quad \\text{not an integer}\n$$\n\nSo 89 is a **prime factor**.\n\nNow factor 4581.\n\nTry 3:\n\n$$\n4581 \\div 3 = 1527\n$$\n\nTry 3 again:\n\n$$\n1527 \\div 3 = 509\n$$\n\nNow check if 509 is prime.\n\nTry dividing 509 by primes up to √509 ≈ 22.56:\n\n- 509 ÷ 2 = no\n- 509 ÷ 3 = 169.66… no\n- 509 ÷ 5 = no\n- 509 ÷ 7 = no\n- 509 ÷ 11 = no\n- 509 ÷ 13 = no\n- 509 ÷ 17 = no\n- 509 ÷ 19 = no\n- 509 ÷ 23 = no\n\nSo **509 is prime**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Prime Factorization of 407707\n\nFrom above:\n\n- 407707 = 89 × 4581\n- 4581 = 3 × 3 × 509\n- So, 407707 = 89 × 3 × 3 × 509\n\nThus, the **prime factors** of 407707 are:\n\n- 3, 3, 89, 509\n\nSo the **unique prime factors** are: **3, 89, 509**\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Largest and Second-Largest Prime Factors\n\n- Largest: 509\n- Second-largest: 89\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Compute the Positive Difference\n\n$$\n509 - 89 = \\boxed{420}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{420}\n$$",
